# camofox.env.example — copy to $CAMOFOX_ROOT/.env (or anywhere) and point
# CAMOFOX_ENV_FILE at it:
#
#   cp camofox.env.example "${REPL_HOME:-$HOME}/camofox/.env"
#   # ...or keep it elsewhere and be explicit:
#   export CAMOFOX_ENV_FILE=/path/to/camofox.env
#
# Both start-camofox.sh and camofox.py load it. Resolution order is exactly:
#   1. $CAMOFOX_ENV_FILE
#   2. $CAMOFOX_ROOT/.env   (tool-native home; start-camofox.sh sets
#      CAMOFOX_ROOT to ${REPL_HOME:-$HOME}/camofox — REPL_HOME is the
#      persistent workspace, $HOME is wiped on restart)
#   3. the plain process environment
# Nothing else is consulted — no agent framework, no implicit home dirs.
#
# EVERY variable below can live in this file, not just the key: it is loaded
# BEFORE any setting is read (start-camofox.sh with `set -a`, camofox.py at
# import). Later duplicates within the file win over earlier ones.
#
# Precedence vs the shell differs between the two tools — verified, not a bug:
#   camofox.py       -> the AMBIENT env wins over the file (setdefault merge)
#   start-camofox.sh -> the FILE wins (defaults exported first, then sourced)
# Keep this file as the single source of truth and export overrides in the
# shell only when you mean them for camofox.py alone.
#
# EVERY variable below is OPTIONAL. Camofox has its own defaults for all of
# them; the commented value after each name is Camofox's default, and an
# uncommented value is the tuned setting this skill recommends. Uncomment only
# what you want to change.

# --- auth ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required when the server runs NODE_ENV=production (loopback cookie import is
# 403 without it). Default: unset = unauthenticated mode.
# CAMOFOX_API_KEY=

# --- keep-alive timers (see references/session-keepalive.md) -------------------
# Per-tab inactivity reaper. Camofox default 300000 (5min) sits exactly on a
# 300s client loop period, so the reaper wins and closes the tab. 900000 = 15min
# gives a 3x margin. NOTE: 0 does NOT disable this one — lib/config.js:149 is
# `parseInt(...) || 300000`, so 0 is falsy and silently becomes 300000 (the most
# aggressive). Use a large number (86400000 = 24h) to effectively disable it.
# CAMOFOX_DEFAULT: 300000
# TAB_INACTIVITY_MS=900000

# Session reaper — the REAL binding constraint (a tab reap empties the session,
# which then closes and drops the login). Camofox default 600000 (10min). Unlike
# the tab reaper, 0 here genuinely disables expiry (`SESSION_TIMEOUT_MS > 0` at
# server.js:5978).
# CAMOFOX_DEFAULT: 600000
# SESSION_TIMEOUT_MS=1800000

# Idle browser shutdown. Camofox default 300000 (5min) means a cold start
# (~90s: xvfb + camoufox launch) the next time a run needs the browser. Only
# runs when sessions.size === 0. 0 = never shut it down.
# CAMOFOX_DEFAULT: 300000
# BROWSER_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS=0

# --- port ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Camofox already defaults to 9377 (lib/config.js:129 tries CAMOFOX_PORT, then
# PORT, then '9377'). Only set this if you need a different port, or if
# something else in the environment exports PORT.
# ⚠️ If you change it, change CAMOFOX_URL below to match: the server listens on
# this one and the client dials that one, so setting only one silently breaks
# every request.
# CAMOFOX_DEFAULT: 9377
# CAMOFOX_PORT=9377

# --- client (camofox.py only) --------------------------------------------------
# Where the CLI looks for the server. Camofox itself does NOT read this — it is
# a client-side setting, and start-camofox.sh does not need it.
# CAMOFOX_DEFAULT: http://127.0.0.1:9377
# CAMOFOX_URL=http://127.0.0.1:9377

# --- paths --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Everything defaults to one root: ${REPL_HOME:-$HOME}/camofox, where REPL_HOME
# is the persistent Replit workspace (/home/runner/workspace) and $HOME is the
# fallback off Replit. Override only if you want the provision tree elsewhere
# (all four move together).
# NOTE: CAMOFOX_ROOT here is honoured by the tools, but the file that CONTAINS
# this line is located from the ambient $CAMOFOX_ROOT, since the path must be
# known before the file is read. To relocate the tree, export CAMOFOX_ROOT in
# the shell (or set it in .replit [userenv]) rather than here.
# CAMOFOX_DEFAULT: ${REPL_HOME:-$HOME}/camofox
# CAMOFOX_ROOT=
# CAMOFOX_DEFAULT: $CAMOFOX_ROOT/camofox-browser
# CAMOFOX_REPO_DIR=
# CAMOFOX_DEFAULT: $CAMOFOX_ROOT/camoufox
# CAMOUFOX_INSTALL_DIR=
# CAMOFOX_DEFAULT: $CAMOFOX_ROOT/state
# CAMOFOX_STATE_DIR=
